{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/202973-introducing-the-setting-through-play","id":202973,"title":"Introducing the setting through play","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-07-20T08:43:27-07:00","id":202973,"title":"Introducing the setting through play","content":"I'm going to be storytelling a Changeling game in my local tabletop roleplaying club, so we'll probably have a lot of newbies, if not the whole motley of newbies. No doubt some of the people on the board already have experience teaching the ctl setting through the game. Any advice on that? I have the freehold worked out, but I don't think my usual sandbox thing will work with newbies...<br /> So, tips?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3316-cantshutup","name":"cantshutup","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-20T12:03:02-07:00","id":203107,"title":"","content":"I have mastered changeling a couple of times and taking into account your group these are my tips. When it comes to newbies who don't have any experience my advice is to start with a linear adventure and to summarize the setting. The reason is simple, your players wont be able to enjoy a sandbox experience if they don't know what the game has to offer, what their characters can do and how does the world work. An introductory adventure in which you present situations in which they have the chance to learn about what means to be a changeling and what changelings can do is perfect. Then as they learn more and get a handle on their characters you can give them more freedom till you just have to act as a guide and not hold their hands any more. I hope my advice helps you <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-20T14:43:38-07:00","id":203259,"title":"","content":"My favorite &quot;scene&quot; to start a changeling game with, especially for newbies, would be any party at the freehold. A season changing from one to another is always good, as you can introduce a lot of the NPCs, what they do, and give a lot of flavor to two of the courts. In one game, I used this as the setting/opening scene, and I had the PCs motley &quot;get a job&quot; to go help find something in the hedge from another attendee. Good way to show them the social side, and then go into the hedge for some weirdness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2734-atwannabe","name":"ATwannabe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2734_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-20T16:48:03-07:00","id":203308,"title":"","content":"I've found that for new players it really helps to start them off as either having to escape from the Hedge and safely make it to the Freehold where they're presented with a clear antagonist to overcome to succeed, or where they're already members of the Freehold but a completely new Motley that's given a mission by the current ruling Monarchy. In either case they should still be presented with a clear antagonist but in a way that makes them wonder what's really going on. For the former perhaps they're hunted by Privateers and learn that they cater to a particularly nasty member of the Gentry who can be the main villain in a later Chronicle. For the later an assassin could be going around the Freehold murdering key figures of a particular Court and the mystery could be whether the murderer is under oath to a hidden Loyalist or perhaps a greedy member of a rival Courts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}